\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces \small \add@extra@listi {sml}\textbf {Robustness check, Specification 1 (baseline ordering), sample 2007--2014.} The figure shows the responses of the endogenous variables to an increase in immigration sentiment, as reflected in speeches by members of the opposition parties (horizons 0--50). Shaded areas denote 68\% credible intervals. All impulse responses are obtained from a recursively identified Bayesian VAR model with one lag and Normal--Wishart priors.}}{40}{figure.23}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces \small \add@extra@listi {sml}\textbf {Robustness check, Specification 2 (reordered macroeconomic block), sample 2007--2014.} The figure shows the responses of the endogenous variables to an increase in immigration sentiment, as reflected in speeches by members of the opposition parties (horizons 0--50). Shaded areas denote 68\% credible intervals. All impulse responses are obtained from a recursively identified Bayesian VAR model with one lag and Normal--Wishart priors.}}{41}{figure.24}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {25}{\ignorespaces \small \add@extra@listi {sml}\textbf {Robustness check, Specification 3 (sentiment ordered second), sample 2007--2014.} The figure shows the responses of the endogenous variables to an increase in immigration sentiment, as reflected in speeches by members of the opposition parties (horizons 0--50). Shaded areas denote 68\% credible intervals. All impulse responses are obtained from a recursively identified Bayesian VAR model with one lag and Normal--Wishart priors.}}{42}{figure.25}%
